      "content": "It can be painful to acknowledge the limitations and cessation of something that defined you for so long. In this space, you're not just stopping the engine, you're also stopping the narratives and roles that were tied to it. This surrender can be a form of self-release, freeing you from the burdens and identities that no longer serve you. Remember, maintaining something once its purpose is gone can be crippling; sometimes, letting go is the most revolutionary act of self-love.",
      "source": "target",
